00:36:47.680 --> 00:36:48.660
y, z,

00:36:48.660 --> 00:36:49.780
some other things.

00:36:49.780 --> 00:36:53.620
But we just need an arbitrary
number of these inputs, so we've

00:36:53.620 --> 00:36:55.220
indexed them off.

00:36:55.220 --> 00:36:57.540
Now, what I'm getting at is this

00:36:57.540 --> 00:37:03.380
model form sort of

00:37:03.380 --> 00:37:06.320
looks like a dot product

00:37:06.320 --> 00:37:10.520
between a parameter vector that
has all of my w's in it,

00:37:10.880 --> 00:37:15.100
with the vector xi.

00:37:15.780 --> 00:37:19.200
But it's not exactly that.

00:37:19.200 --> 00:37:22.950
Because there are only d
features,

00:37:23.080 --> 00:37:27.580
but there are d plus one
parameters.

00:37:28.040 --> 00:37:31.480
So there's something we have to
do here.

00:37:31.480 --> 00:37:32.780
I guess what I'm getting at is
this.

00:37:32.780 --> 00:37:34.700
Our parameter vector

00:37:34.700 --> 00:37:40.700
has d plus 1

00:37:40.700 --> 00:37:41.700
