the intercept term which doesn't

00:38:35.320 --> 00:38:39.780
multiply an X itself It just has
to exist

00:38:39.780 --> 00:38:40.780
So

00:38:42.160 --> 00:38:49.660
W which is in R D plus 1 is our
parameter vector

00:38:50.520 --> 00:38:58.020
X I which is in R D is a feature
vector

00:38:58.360 --> 00:39:04.320
And the augmented feature vector
is in R

00:39:04.320 --> 00:39:06.480
d plus 1.
And it can be dotted with the

00:39:06.480 --> 00:39:07.480
parameter.

00:39:12.760 --> 00:39:16.510
And these features can be
whatever we want them to be,

00:39:16.720 --> 00:39:20.440
including arbitrary functions of
the original features of the

00:39:20.440 --> 00:39:21.980
data set, or squares,

00:39:21.980 --> 00:39:22.480
cubes,

00:39:22.480 --> 00:39:24.020
signs, whatever you want.

00:39:24.020 --> 00:39:26.900
As long as your model can be
separated in this form,

00:39:26.900 --> 00:39:28.400
you're fine.

00:39:29.240 --> 00:39:30.980
So as you mentioned earlier,

00:39:30.980 --> 00:39:33.940
this tells us the general shape
of the design matrix

00:39:33.940 --> 00:39:39.160
