you add them up,

00:51:24.720 --> 00:51:28.080
these also give you 1, 1, 1, 1,

00:51:28.080 --> 00:51:29.080
1.

00:51:34.320 --> 00:51:38.820
sum, but that is a linear
combination,

00:51:39.440 --> 00:51:42.140
or sorry, this linear
combination of this column plus

00:51:42.140 --> 00:51:44.840
this plus this plus this plus
this gives you the intercept

00:51:44.840 --> 00:51:47.060
column of all the ones.

00:51:47.060 --> 00:51:50.240
What that means is the columns
of your design matrix then are

00:51:50.240 --> 00:51:52.160
no longer linearly independent,

00:51:52.160 --> 00:51:54.060
and so x transpose x doesn't,

00:51:54.060 --> 00:51:56.060
inverse doesn't exist.

00:51:56.060 --> 00:51:59.540
Does that mean there is no
optimal parameter vector? No, it

00:51:59.540 --> 00:52:00.980
doesn't mean that.
It means there are infinitely

00:52:00.980 --> 00:52:03.780
many optimal parameter vectors.

00:52:03.780 --> 00:52:07.000
There is always at least one
optimal parameter vector because

00:52:07.000 --> 00:52:10.580
there is always some way to make
the closest predictions.

00:52:10.580 --> 00:52:12.660
The question is, is there only
one way to do that or infinitely

00:52:12.660 --> 00:52:15.520
many ways to do that?

00:52:15.520 --> 00:52:18.960
And when we keep all five of
these columns, then there are

00:52:18.960 --> 00:52:21.840
infinitely many solutions to, if
you recall, we call this the

00:52:21.840 --> 00:52:23.340
normal equation.

00:52:24.020 --> 00:52:29.120
What do you think a remedy to
this is?

00:52:29.120 --> 00:52:32.480
What's a solution to this?

00:52:32.480 --> 00:52:34.730
We give up.

00:52:35.080 --> 00:52:40.140
Well, we're going to give up a
little, not completely.

00:52:40.140 --> 00:52:42.260
What we give up is what?

00:52:42.260 --> 00:52:43.260
Exactly.

00:52:43.640 --> 00:52:45.800
We just give up on caring if
it's Friday or not.

00:52:45.800 --> 00:52:48.020
If we remove the Friday column,

00:52:48.020 --> 00:52:49.320
you realize you don't really
need it.

00:52:49.320 --> 00:52:51.480
Because if it's not Monday,
Tuesday, Wednesday, or Thursday,

00:52:51.480 --> 00:52:53.740
it had to be Friday.

00:52:53.740 --> 00:52:55.500
Conceptually, that makes sense.

00:52:55.500 --> 00:52:56.500
Mathematically,

00:52:56.640 --> 00:53:00.540
this Friday column still exists
in the span of the columns of

00:53:00.540 --> 00:53:03.700
the design matrix, because that
Friday column is just the ones

00:53:03.700 --> 00:53:06.900
column minus Monday, Tuesday,
Wednesday, or Thursday's

00:53:06.900 --> 00:53:07.900
columns.

00:53:08.920 --> 00:53:11.920
So that's the solution.
You drop one of the categories.

00:53:12.020 --> 00:53:14.160
And again, you're going to
explore this in coming

00:53:14.160 --> 00:53:15.160
